---
title: Spicy Beef and Bean Chili
source: direct-input
description: A pepper-packed chili with a fresh lime finish and optional beans, based on 1.5 lb of beef.
tags: [chili, beef, spicy]
---

> This batch uses 1.5 lb of ground beef. Beans are optional; use kidney beans or pinto beans. Serranos may replace the habaneros. Reserve any salsa before adding the meat.

Add @garlic{1%bulb}(diced small) and @onion{1-2}(whole, red or yellow, or mixed; diced) to @oil{} and simmer until it begins to steam.

Add @jalapenos{10}(chopped finely) and @habaneros{10}(or serranos; chopped finely), and let it simmer for a bit.

Add @roma tomatoes{10-15}(chopped finely) and the spices: @cumin{1%tbsp}, @paprika{2%tsp}, about @garlic powder{3%tbsp}, @onion powder{2%tsp}, @pepper flakes{1%tsp}, @MSG{4-5%tbsp}, about @salt{0.5%tbsp}, and @pepper{} to taste. Let it simmer until most of the excess water has boiled away.

Reserve however much of the salsa you want before adding the meat.

Add @ground beef{1.5%lb} and, if using, @?kidney beans{1%can}(or pinto beans). Add @chilli powder{3%tbsp}. Mix well, breaking up the beef, and simmer for about ~{15%minutes}, until the beef is fully cooked and the chili has reached the desired thickness.

Finish with @limes{4}(juiced), then serve.
